          "code": "SHOWJOBDETAILS",
          "id": "1767017092086",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767017092087_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "JobData : {{$context.$nodes.FINDJOBDETAILSBYCODE.$output.items[0]}}\n\n\nYour goal is to show below mentioned table sections:\n\n## A. Mandatory Table Sections:\n\n1. Create a new table having 2 columns:\n * Section header will be Job Details:\n * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n * First column will have attribute name(40% width), second column will have data(60% width).\n * Job Details :{{$context.$nodes.FINDJOBDETAILSBYCODE.$output.items}}\n         Only show fields EffectiveStartDate as Effective Start Date, EffectiveEndDate as Effective End Date, SetName as Set, JobName as Job Name, JobCode as Job Code, ActiveStatusMeaning as Status, JobFamilyName as Job Family, JobSubFamilyMeaning  as Job SubFamily, JobFunctionCodeMeaning as Job Function, RegularTemporaryMeaning  as Regular or Temporary, FullPartTimeMeaning as Full Time or Part Time. \n* MUST ensure proper HTML table tags are generated.\n\n2. Create another new table having 3 columns:\n  * MUST ensure proper HTML table tags are generated.\n * Section header will be Valid Grades:\n * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n * First column will have attribute Serial No.(20%width), second column will have Attribute.(40%width) and third column will have Data.(40%width).\n * Valid Grades : {{$context.$nodes.FINDJOBDETAILSBYCODE.$output.items[0].validGrades}}\n         Here, in Serial No. column just show Row No. and in Attribute show field Grade Name, Grade Code, Grade Set in multiple lines under same row and respective values in Data. Show multiple records in multiple rows with row no. as attribute.\n * Branching rule to add(Not to be displayed)\n  - If 0 results:  show “No valid grades found.”  text, and terminate ,do not show an empty table for zero results.\n\n\nMANDATORY: \n* Show results strictly in HTML table with proper border and style.\n* For any HTML table style the table header row with background: medium gray;\n* For any HTML table STRICTLY make sure it always includes visible borders around all cells and border style as border-collapse: collapse;\n* Strictly follow above commands and display data with proper width, borders and rules defined.\n* Give proper spacing between 2 sections.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 9125,
            "y": 8758
          }
