          "code": "FINDEFFECTIVESTARTDATEFORSUMMARY",
          "id": "1767068059432",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767068059434_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "UserInput : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nHistoryRecords: {{$context.$nodes.INVOKEJOBHISTORYFORSUMMARY.$output.items}}\n\nif user has mentioned a single date in UserInput:\n    --UserRequestDateStart :  Extract user request date from UserInput otherwise save {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} as UserRequestDate.\n    --UserRequestDateEnd : Save {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} as UserRequestDateEnd.\nif user has not mentioned any date in UserInput:\n    --UserRequestDateStart :  Save {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} as UserRequestDateStart.\n    --UserRequestDateEnd : Save {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} as UserRequestDateEnd.\nIf user wants to view modified attributes between date range in system, then\n     eg: User: \"Show me the modification done between 01-January 2020 to 01-January 2025 of Job Admin.\"\n    --UserRequestDateStart: Extract Starting date for this date range and store as UserRequestDateStart.\n    --UserRequestDateEnd: Extract ending date for this date range and store as UserRequestDateEnd. \n\n\n\n** Identify RangeStart and  RangeEnd based on UserRequestDate:\n      Rule: From HistoryRecords select records falling on or after the extracted UserRequestDateStart and on or before the extracted UserRequestDateEnd. Skip history record having FirstDESplitFlag true.\n      --Extract EffectiveStartDate value from each selected HistoryRecords as per Rule and store as String in an Array.\n      --Return the Array as selectedEffectiveStartDates.\n\n**If user has asked a comparison between previous version to latest version\n     Rule: From HistoryRecords select last record and extract EffectiveStartDate value from the selected HistoryRecords and store as String in an Array. Skip history record having FirstDESplitFlag true.\n       --Return the Array as selectedEffectiveStartDates.\n\n**Example Response**:\n->return selectedEffectiveStartDates = [\"2024-01-01\",\"2025-01-01\",\"2025-10-01\"]"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"selectedEffectiveStartDates\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8112.5,
            "y": 8980
          }
        },
