          "code": "AGGREGATECHANGES",
          "id": "1767068414550",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767068414553_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Goal: Present Job modifications from the following data source:\nModificationsOnJob : {{$context.$nodes.ITERATEOVERRANGEFORSUMMARY.$output}}\n\n**Example ModificationsOnJob format***\n{\n  \"EffectiveStartDate\": <value>,\n  \"ChangeSummary\": [\n    {\n      \"UserAttributeName\": \"JobFamily\",\n      \"AfterValue\": \"Admin\",\n      \"BeforeValue\": \"Executive\",\n      \"@context\": {\"key\": \"1\"}\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\n**Display requirements**\n- Show the message above the table: Here’s a summary of the changes made.\n- Then display only an HTML table of the identified modifications. Do not include any other summary or text.\n- Table columns (in this order and with these headers):\n  - Effective Start Date (source: EffectiveStartDate)\n  - What Changed (source: ChangeSummary[].UserAttributeName)\n  - After (source: ChangeSummary[].AfterValue)\n  - Before (source: ChangeSummary[].BeforeValue)\n- Group rows by EffectiveStartDate. For consecutive entries with the same EffectiveStartDate, merge the cells in the “Effective Start Date” column into a single cell (use proper HTML rowspan), treating the merged set as one row for counting merged cells.\n- Styling and borders (strict):\n  - Use a visible border around all cells with border-collapse: collapse.\n  - Header row background: medium gray;\n  - Ensure proper width and consistent borders for all cells.\n\n**Rendering rules**\n-If a record has an empty or missing ChangeSummary, skip it (no rows).\n-If AfterValue or BeforeValue is missing, render an empty cell.\n-Always render a single header row once, followed by all data rows.\n\n**Finalization**\n- After the table, say Thank you. and end."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8112.5,
            "y": 9922
