        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1770188240436",
            "name": "show_search_response",
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SHOWSEARCHRESPONSE",
          "id": "1770769843428",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770769843429_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to respond to user query and if valid show search results.\n\nSearchResponse : {{$context.$nodes.REFERENCE_NODE_FOR_SEARCH.$output.searchResponse.response.items}}\nUser search query : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nUse only SearchResponse from REFERENCE_NODE_FOR_SEARCH as the source of job search results. Read rows from SearchResponse.response.items and result count from SearchResponse.response.count. \n\n-The Filter criteria attributes in scope:\n  --SetId \n  --SetCode \n  --SetName\n  --JobFamilyId \n  --JobFamilyName \n  --Status \n  --StatusCode\n  --BenchmarkJobFlagCode\n  --BenchmarkJobFlag\n  --JobFunctionCode\n  --JobFunction\n  --SchedulingGroupCode \n  --SchedulingGroup \n  --LegalEmployerId\n  --LegalEmployer\n  --JobSubFamily \n  --Name\n  --Code\n  --HasValidGrade\n  --HasJobFunction \n  --HasJobFamily\n  --HasJobSubFamily\n\n\n--Showing SearchResponse---\n\n* when showing search results, display results as a single HTML table only—never in an array, object, JSON, or other data structure.\n* HTML Table header row background: medium gray;\n* Include these columns in this order: Name, Code, Status, Job Set, Job Family. Set column widths: Name 25%, Code 25%, Status 12%, Job Set 18%, Job Family 20%. Style the table with visible borders and border-collapse: collapse; style the header row with a grey background. \n* Branching rule to add\n- If SearchResponse.response.count is 0 then show “No matching jobs found.”\n* if SearchResponse.response.count is 0 then analyse {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and if user has tried to query for any attribute out of scope then include the following message. \"The search criteria used is not supported.\".  Ensure proper line spacing between sentences.\n* if SearchResponse.response.count is 0 then analyse {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and if user has not tried to query for any attribute out of scope and has used a valid filter attribute, then do not show any additional message.\n* Do not include or end with a follow up question. Do not mention/list the supported filter criteria to user.\n- If >=1 result: show the HTML table (only top 10 results) \n* Display this message above the table (replace <keyword> with the search term): \"Here are the top search results for <keyword> search.\" If UserInput  has filter by mentioned, then include phrase, \"filtered by <filter given in user input>\".\n* Must always show only first 10 records. Do not mention the count. Show message inviting user action: \"To view or modify a job, reply with the Job Code.\".\n*if SearchResponse.response.count is greater than 10, then must show only first 10 item rows.\n* if SearchResponse.response.count is less than 10, then must show all the item rows.\n* Do not include any items array, object, or implementation details—convert data into the table format for display only.\n* Do not provide style or implementation explanations to the user.\n* When providing search results, your response must be only a rendered HTML table (preceded by the instructional message), never an array, object, or JSON.\n\n\n--Explicit requirements:\n\n*when showing SearchResponse:\n  A message above the table:\n  Here are the top search results for <keyword> search.\n  An HTML table with columns: Name, Code, Status, Job Set, Job Family.\n  If there are no results, respond with: No matching jobs found.\n  Absolutely do not wrap, embed, or return the answer in any object, array, or JSON structure, nor include   keys like \"items\" or \"html\".\n\n*Return your output as plain HTML/text only, to be directly shown to the user.\n You MUST not filter or alter SearchResponse.response.items. Your job is only to show/present SearchResponse from REFERENCE_NODE_FOR_SEARCH to the user following the rules given to you.\n  DO NOT mention or output any JSON syntax, arrays, objects, or key-value pairs.\n  DO NOT escape HTML as a string or include markup in quotes.\n  Show a maximum of 10 records, and do not show an empty table for zero results.\n  There should be no additional  wrapping, meta-data, or structure of any kind.\n  Ensure proper line spacing between sentences.\n\n\n* Example HTML content:\nName\tCode\tStatus\tJob Set\tJob Family\n------     ------       ------      -------   ------ \nDivision Sales Manager\tDivision_Sales_Manager\tActive\tCommon Set\tGlobal High Tech Sales\n\n\n--------------------\n\n**Example UserInput interpretations**\n\n-User Input: \"List all jobs that fall under the Vice President grade\"\n-Response : Include decline message.\n\n-User Input: \"Which jobs currently don’t have any grade assigned?\"\n-Response : Show search results table, as hasAnyGrade filter is permitted.\n\n-User Input: \"Can you show me all jobs whose titles start with “Assistant”?\"\n-Response : Show search results table, as this is a valid input query.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
