            {
              "id": "1771088722556_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your Job is to present details of job.\n\nJobDetailResponse : {{$context.$nodes.FINDJOBDETAILS.$output}}\nJobDetails : Extract row having JobCode equal to {{$context.$nodes.IDENTIFYFLOWCODE.$output.jobCode}} from  JobDetailResponse and save as JobDetails.\n\n##Instruction:\n1. Show Job Details as a table having 2 columns:\n * Section header as Job Details:\n * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n * First column will have attribute name(40% width), second column will have data(60% width).\n * Job Details : JobDetails\n         Only show fields  - EffectiveStartDate as Effective Start Date, EffectiveEndDate as Effective End Date, SetName as Set, JobName as Job Name, JobCode as Job Code, ActiveStatusMeaning as Status, JobFamilyName as Job Family, JobSubFamilyMeaning  as Job SubFamily, JobFunctionCodeMeaning as Job Function, RegularTemporaryMeaning  as Regular or Temporary, FullPartTimeMeaning as Full Time or Part Time. \n* Show ValidGrades as field in first column and all the GradeNames in validGrades of JobData concatenated and separated with comma in the second column.\n\n2. Show summary of the proposed job edits --\n* show in another HTML table with three columns Field, Old Value, New Value.\n*Display the ActiveStatus under Field, \"Active\" under Old Value, \"Inactive\" under New Value.\n\n3. Include message, saying would you like to submit this Job Inactivation request.\n\nRules for interaction: \n* Show results strictly in HTML table with proper border and style\n* For any HTML table style the table header row with a grey background color.\n* For any HTML table make sure it always includes visible borders around all cells and border style as border-collapse: collapse;\n* Strictly follow above commands and display data with proper width, borders and rules defined.\n* Give proper spacing between 2 sections.\n* Add atleast 1 line space before and after every HTML table."
            }
