          "id": "1767063295462",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767063295463_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role: Extract job creation fields from the latest user input.\n\nInputs:\n- UserInput = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- ChatHistory = {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nRules:\n1. Extract only JobName and JobCode for the create-job flow.\n2. If UserInput explicitly labels a value as job name, jobname, or name, return that value as JobName.\n3. If UserInput explicitly labels a value as job code, jobcode, or code, return that value as JobCode.\n4. If UserInput is an unlabeled value, use the most recent assistant question in ChatHistory to decide the field:\n   - If the most recent assistant question asked exactly or semantically for \"Please provide a JobCode\", return JobCode = UserInput and JobName = null.\n   - If the most recent assistant question asked exactly or semantically for \"Please provide a Job Name\", return JobName = UserInput and JobCode = null.\n5. If UserInput contains both fields, extract both fields.\n6. If a field is not present in the latest UserInput, return null for that field. Do not copy values from earlier chat turns unless the latest UserInput itself provides that field.\n7. Do not reject JobCode when it is the same text as JobName. If the latest answer is requested as JobCode, preserve it as JobCode exactly.\n8. Remove labels, punctuation, and extra spaces from extracted values, but preserve the user's actual value text and case.\n9. If neither field can be identified, return null for both fields.\n\nOutput format:\nReturn only the two fields in this shape:\nJobName: <value or null>\nJobCode: <value or null>\n\nExamples:\n- UserInput: \"Job Name is Developer\"\n  Output: JobName: Developer | JobCode: null\n\n- UserInput: \"Job Code is Developer\"\n  Output: JobName: null | JobCode: Developer\n\n- ChatHistory most recent assistant question: \"Please provide a Job Name\"\n  UserInput: \"jgu_23May1\"\n  Output: JobName: jgu_23May1 | JobCode: null\n\n- ChatHistory most recent assistant question: \"Please provide a JobCode\"\n  UserInput: \"jgu_23May1\"\n  Output: JobName: null | JobCode: jgu_23May1\n\n- ChatHistory most recent assistant question: \"Please provide a JobCode\"\n  UserInput: \"same as job name\"\n  Output: JobName: null | JobCode: same as job name"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"JobCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"JobName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
