          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767064102072_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Show Job Creation details"
            },
            {
              "id": "1767064102072_2",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your job is to inform user that create has been completed successfully with details of the Job created.\n\nif {{$context.$variables.jobCodeGenMethod}} is \"M\" then:\nJobCreation response : {{$context.$nodes.INVOKECREATEWITHJOBCODE.$output}}. \nJobCreation responseStatus : {{$context.$nodes.INVOKECREATEWITHJOBCODE.$status }}.\n\nelse if {{$context.$variables.jobCodeGenMethod}} is not \"M\" then:\nJobCreation response : {{$context.$nodes.INVOKEJOBSCREATE.$output}}.  \nJobCreation responseStatus : {{$context.$nodes.INVOKEJOBSCREATE.$status }}\n\n**Objective**: Notify the user of a successfully completed job creation process.\n\nResponse Logic:\n\n1. If JobCreation responseStatus is 204, inform the user: \"The job has been successfully submitted for creation.\" Do not mention \"View Job\" in this case.\n\n2. If JobCreation responseStatus is 201 and JobCreation response includes a valid JobId in the payload, display the job details and provide a link to view_job. Then, gracefully terminate the process.\n\n--Formatting the Response if JobCreation responseStatus is 201:\n\n        -----Always display the response data in an HTML table with borders and two columns, without a header row.\n\n        -----The first column will include these labels: EffectiveStartDate, JobId, JobName, JobCode, SetName \n\n        -----The second column will show the corresponding values retrieved from the JobCreation output, exactly as returned in the response—do not rephrase values.\n\n\n** Functions **\n\n1. view_job_link: Must be invoked to provide deeplink to view job page."
            }
          ],
          "type": "AGENT",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5225,
            "y": 10810
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
