        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "AskUserInputForCreate"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ASKUSERINPUTFORCREATE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767062858085",
          "id": "1767062559737",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767062559738_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "JobName : {{$context.$variables.JobName}}\nJobCode :  {{$context.$variables.JobCode}}\nJobCodeGenMethod : {{$context.$variables.jobCodeGenMethod}}\n\nYour Job is to collect required attributes to create a new job.\n\n##Instructions##\n1. If JobName is empty or null then ask user to provide a JobName to create the Job. Ask exactly \"Please provide a Job Name\".\n2. If JobCodeGenMethod is \"M\" and if JobCode is empty or null then ask user to provide a JobCode to create the Job. Ask exactly \"Please provide a JobCode\"."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5787.5,
            "y": 9202
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "specification": {
              "agentRole": "Professional",
              "inputs": [],
              "outputSpecification": "",
              "summarizationMode": "Custom",
              "summarizationPrompt": "Based on the information through the chat history and/or tool call responses, construct a clear, professional, and user-friendly answer to address the user's original query.\nconstruct an answer that addresses the user's original query.\nYour answer should be directed towards the user and should be friendly, professional,\nand concise. If you are not able to answer the user's question based on the tool calls or through the chat history,\nyou should let them know that you do not have access to that information.\n\n--ANSWER REQUIREMENTS--\nYour answer should be based only on the information available to you in the tool calling chat\nhistory. You should never invent or make up answers. If the question requires you to synthesize\nanswers across several tool responses, you should do that. Note that some information may need\nto be summarized from across multiple places in a given object. Use your inference and semantic\nknowledge to derive the answer from the data without inventing anything.\n\n--ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS--\n* Do not mention tool calls, chat history, underlying operations, or system processes.\n* Keep the response natural and conversational without unnecessary preambles.\n* Provide a direct and engaging response without phrases like \"Based on tool calls\" or similar references.\n* Do not append any characters or trailing Periods (.) at the end of valid URLs.\n* If link is generated by DeepLink tool do not remove from response.\n* Ensure proper full stop, line spacing and new lines are added.\n\n--- Answering Guidelines ---\n\n  * Phrase attributes in natural language (e.g., \"The job is X\" instead of \"Job: X\").\n  * Do not just return \"label: value\"; always phrase it into a complete, user-friendly response.\n  * For any HTML table style the table header row with a light grey background colour always.\n  * For any HTML table make sure it always includes visible borders around all cells and border style as border-collapse: collapse;\n  * For any HTML table, do not show null values. Show blank column for null values. \n  * If multiple rows/objects exist, always present them in a table.Use style=\"table-layout: auto; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;\". Ensure spacing and wrapping for readability.\n  * When you display the variable name, you must convert the CamelCase variable name into a readable label with spaces for human readability. Id should be shown as ID (e.g., JobId as Job ID).\n  * For general queries and responses that does not require user response or when terminating, close mentioning \"Happy to help with any Job related actions !\"\n  * Present the summary as a short, brief bullet list.\n  * Ensure spacing and wrapping for readability.\n  * Provide professional, concise, human-friendly responses.\n * STRICTLY view job url must be provided from view_job_link DeepLink tool response only. view_job_link DeepLink tool response must never be referred from chat history.\n  * Ensure each sentence ends with a Period(.).\n  * Never display more than 2 sentence in a paragraph.\n  * Add atleast two line space before and after any HTML tables.\n  * Always add view_job_link response at the end of the sentence.\n\n--Showing findHistory --\n* Section header as History:\n * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n* Always show in HTML table with columns as Effective Start Date, Effective End Date, Changed Attributes.\n* Show Row number column without any column header. \n\n--Showing JobDetails --\n* Always show in HTML table with two columns without a header row.\n* First Column should contain below mentioned values.\n- JobName as Job Name, JobCode as Job Code, ActiveStatusMeaning as Status, SetName as Set, JobFamilyName as Job Family, JobSubFamilyMeaning  as Job SubFamily, JobFunctionCodeMeaning as Job Function, RegularTemporaryMeaning  as Regular or Temporary, FullPartTimeMeaning as Full Time or Part Time. \n* Second Column should contain the corresponding values of the fields mentioned in field column fetched from JobDetails output. Value should be shown exactly as returned by JobDetails response. DO NOT rephrase values.\n* Do not include validGrades.\n* When displaying JobDetails, include the message: “Here are the details for the <Job Name> Job” above the table.\n\n-- Answering delete/remove job request --\n1. Show findHistory table.\n2. Show JobDetails table.\n3. When answering delete job request with view_job_link, \n      -- If the findHistory response returns exactly one row (count = 1) then deletion from the view job page is not allowed, respond with: \"There are no records of the job <JobName> that can be deleted. \\n If you wish to  view the details of the job, view <Deeplink URL>\" \n      -- If the findHistory response contains more than one row (count > 1) then, deletion from the view job page is allowed, respond with :  \"You can view the job’s history details at <Deeplink URL>. \\n Review the records and delete the effective-dated row if needed.\"\n\n--- Response formatting Guidelines ---\n- Write clearly and professionally; use correct grammar, periods, and active voice.\n- Keep responses brief and transactional; avoid long paragraphs.\n- Add atleast two line space before and after any HTML tables.\n- Add concise headings only when they improve clarity.\n- Use bullet points or numbered steps for tasks, options, or key data.\n- Maintain consistent punctuation and spacing with a blank line between sections.\n- Keep tone neutral and direct; avoid filler and repetition.\n- Focus strictly on the requested content; do not add conclusions, next steps, or extra sections.",
              "maxInteractions": 20
            },
            "maxInteractions": 10,
            "toolCodes": [
              "ORA_HCM_PER_VIEW_JOB_LINK",
              "ORA_HCM_PER_JOBS",
              "ORA_HCM_DATE_EFFECTIVE_OBJECT_HISTORY"
            ],
            "topicCodes": [],
            "name": "Delete Job Facilitator",
            "type": "PRIVATE",
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ORA_HCM_JOB_FACILITATOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767070296017",
          "id": "1767071408809",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767071429822_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Show response."
            },
            {
              "id": "1767071429822_2",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to analyse JobHistory data given to you and if valid JobHistory found then provide deep link to the Job record.\n\n\nYour role is to help users by providing the deep-link URL when they want to delete a job.\n\n## Inputs\n- **JobDetails**: {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_RESULT_LLM.$output}}  \n- **DeleteEffectiveDate**: {{$context.$nodes.IDENTIFYFLOWCODE.$output.viewDate}}\n\n## Instructions (follow in order)\n1. Invoke **findHistory** with:\n   - **ObjectId** = {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_RESULT_LLM.$output.JobId}}\n   - **historyDefClassName** = \"oracle.apps.hcm.employment.responsive.publicUiModel.history.definitions.JobHistoryDef\"  \n   Store the response as **HistoryDetails**.\n2. Invoke **view_job_link** function using **JobId** and **EffectiveStartDate** from **JobDetails**.\n3. Show findHistory as HTML table and then JobDetails as another HTML table. Then include summary text based on the following instructions.\n4. If **HistoryDetails** count = 1, provide  view_job_link as link to user and say exactly (do not rephrase):  \n   \"There are no records of the job {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_RESULT_LLM.$output.JobName}} that can be deleted. You can view the details of the Job <view_job_link>.\"  \n   Then terminate.\n5. If **HistoryDetails** count > 1, find the row where **EffectiveStartDate** ≤ **DeleteEffectiveDate** and **EffectiveEndDate** ≥ **DeleteEffectiveDate**. Store it as **identifiedDeleteHistoryRecord**.\n6. If **identifiedDeleteHistoryRecord. FirstSplitFlag** = true, say exactly (do not rephrase):  \n   \"The first Date Effective record of the job <JobName from JobDetails> cannot be deleted.  You can view the details of the Job <view_job_link>.\"  \n   Then terminate.\n7. If **identifiedDeleteHistoryRecord. FirstSplitFlag** = false, invoke **view_job_link** using **JobId** and **EffectiveStartDate** from **JobDetails**, then return the link and say exactly (do not rephrase):  \n   \"You can view the job's history details at <view_job_link>(as URL). Review the records and perform delete if needed.\"\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "AGENT",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 11375,
            "y": 8092
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Evaluate Failure",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const failure = $context.$error;\nconst flow = $context.$workflow.$name;\n\nlet isValid = true;\nlet isErrorAvailable = false;\n\nlet errorMessage = failure.$errorMessage || ''; \nconst nodeName = failure.$nodeCode || ''; \n\nif (typeof errorMessage === 'string' && errorMessage.trim() !== '') {\nlet cleanedMessage = errorMessage.trim();\n  if (cleanedMessage.startsWith('\"') && cleanedMessage.endsWith('\"')) {\n    cleanedMessage = cleanedMessage.slice(1, -1); // Remove outer quotes if present\n  }\n  \n  cleanedMessage = cleanedMessage.replace(/\\\\n/g, '\\n').replace(/\\\\\"/g, '\"');\n  \n  try {\n    const parsedError = JSON.parse(cleanedMessage);\n    \n    if (parsedError['o:errorDetails'] && Array.isArray(parsedError['o:errorDetails']) && parsedError['o:errorDetails'].length > 0) {\n      errorMessage = parsedError['o:errorDetails'][0].detail;\n    }else{\n        errorMessage = parsedError;\n       }\n  } catch (parseError) {\n    errorMessage = cleanedMessage;\n  }\n}\n\nelse if (typeof errorMessage === 'object' && errorMessage !== null) {\n  if (errorMessage['o:errorDetails'] && Array.isArray(errorMessage['o:errorDetails']) && errorMessage['o:errorDetails'].length > 0) {\n    errorMessage = errorMessage['o:errorDetails'][0].detail;\n  } \n    errorMessage = errorMessage;\n}\n\nif (errorMessage && errorMessage !== \"\" && nodeName) {\n  isValid = false;\n  isErrorAvailable = true;\n}\n\nlet errorDetail = {};\nerrorDetail[\"ErrorMessage\"]=errorMessage;\nerrorDetail[\"NodeName\"]=nodeName;\nerrorDetail[\"WorkflowName\"]=flow;\nerrorDetail[\"IsValid\"]=isValid;\nerrorDetail[\"IsErrorAvailable\"]=isErrorAvailable;\n\nreturn errorDetail;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770188280031"
          },
          "code": "EVALUATE_FAILURE",
          "id": "1770188240436",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE",
